This page contains information about the /consider command.

=== Description ===

Considers your current target, which displays an indication of your [[Faction Standing|faction standing]] as well as an indication of the target's relative level and strength.

The target can be specified by name, including pet names, and can use chat variables.

Common abbreviation: /con

The /con check gives you a quick read on how tough a creature is compared to your character. Each color corresponds to a level range, and those ranges determine both danger and expected experience. Most colors follow fixed level gaps, while a few shift slightly depending on your level as described below.

=== Fixed Ranges ===
Red - The target is 4 or more levels above you.
<br>Very dangerous, but excellent experience.

Yellow - 1-3 levels above you.
<br>Challenging, strong experience.

White - Same level as you.
<br>Even match, solid experience.

Dark Blue - 1-5 levels below you.
<br>Manageable fights, still worthwhile experience.

=== Variable Ranges ===
Light Blue - Roughly 6-15 levels below you.
<br>Moderate experience.
<br>Light Blue begins appearing once you reach level 25. The exact point where Light Blue ends (and Green begins) shifts slightly by level.

Green - About 6-20 levels below you.
<br>Minimal experience.
<br>The upper end of Green varies depending on when Grey becomes available for your level.

Grey - Too low to award experience.
<br>Grey appears once a creature is far enough below your level that it no longer grants XP; this threshold changes as you level up.